WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.580
8.

2
00:00:03.440 --> 00:00:09.760
Study-Induced Vulnerability.

3
00:00:09.800 --> 00:00:14.200
Standard participant recruitment can
transition into an active risk

4
00:00:14.240 --> 00:00:17.020
environment depending on the requirements
of the study.

5
00:00:17.700 --> 00:00:21.840
Intrusive study designs and complex
methodologies can directly alter a

6
00:00:21.880 --> 00:00:24.520
participant's psychological or physical
status.

7
00:00:24.980 --> 00:00:29.060
These methods can create or exacerbate
vulnerabilities during the research.

8
00:00:29.460 --> 00:00:33.620
Ultimately, the participant's rights,
welfare, or dignity become actively

9
00:00:33.660 --> 00:00:38.160
compromised. Researchers must maintain
constant vigilance to ensure they do

10
00:00:38.200 --> 00:00:42.200
not unwittingly manufacture the very
exploitation they aim to avoid.

11
00:00:42.720 --> 00:00:46.420
Institutions combat these vulnerabilities
by operationally applying the

12
00:00:46.460 --> 00:00:50.880
Belmont Report principles. Respect for
persons is the obligation to treat

13
00:00:50.920 --> 00:00:54.240
every research participant as an
autonomous decision-maker.

14
00:00:54.640 --> 00:00:59.520
When a population has diminished autonomy,
researchers are required to build

15
00:00:59.560 --> 00:01:01.960
in enhanced structural protections.

16
00:01:02.000 --> 00:01:07.200
this respect is enforced through rigorous
and transparent informed consent

17
00:01:07.240 --> 00:01:07.608
protocols.
